/E (The Earth moves in the plane of the equator; the Sun and Moon, however, move in the plane of the zodiac, an orbit inclined with respect to that of the Earth. This inclination explains the succession of the seasons: the Sun traces an oblique circle as it orbits around the central fire.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
