/P 103 0 R
/E (The Counter-Earth represents one of the most enigmatic aspects of the Philolaic system. Aristotle suggests it was postulated for numerological reasons: with the Counter-Earth, the total number of celestial bodies reaches the perfect number of ten \(together with the Sun, the Moon, the five planets, the Earth, and the sphere of the fixed stars\). However, the Counter-Earth also carries significant astronomical implications.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (A geographical consequence is also that lands beyond the Pillars of Hercules lie in eternal shadow, since the Counter-Earth hides the central fire from that region. Herodotus in fact reports the existence of peoples in the north who sleep for six months a year, as they dwell in perpetual night for half the year.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
