/P 104 0 R
/E (Stobaeus attests that some Pythagoreans believed the visible markings on the Moon were the reflection of the Earth's seas, and others say that for Philolaus the Moon is part of the Earth.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (Philolaus accepts the theories of heliophotism \(that the reflection of sunlight causes the phases of the Moon\) and antiphraxis \(that eclipses are caused by the blocking of sunlight by the Moon or the Earth\). Lunar eclipses occur both when the Moon passes through the shadow of the Earth and when it passes through the shadow of the Counter-Earth.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
