/P 106 0 R
/E (We have said that the concept of the harmony of the spheres is owed to the Pythagoreans: this, together with the discovery that Hesperus, the evening star, and Phosphorus, the morning star, are the same star \(Venus\), may also be discoveries attributable to Parmenides. The attribution of the Pythagorean theorem is analogous: although it bears the name of Pythagoras, the theorem and the corollary concerning the incommensurability of the diagonal of the square are not certainly his original discoveries.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
